From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:18:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 35/40] Online model update: ModelUpdateWorker, debug check,
 REG-EVT-019

The engine's ModelUpdater, run on Android ("model updates securely
synchronized when online"):
- ModelUpdates: the keys mosip.registration.liveness.model.update.enabled
  (default false: no server yet), .url and .intervalHours (default 24).
  The holder schedules, replaces or cancels the unique periodic
  WorkManager job (network connected) at start and after every config
  reload. The job is replaced only when the URL or the interval change.
- ModelUpdateWorker: checks through the running engine
  (LivenessServiceHolder.checkModelUpdate: on INSTALLED a reload, so
  MODEL_LOADED has the new version). If WorkManager started the process
  without the engine, it checks alone, with the same store, assets and
  keys, and keeps the outcome for the engine to audit at its next start.
- One ModelStore instance per process, so installs, rollbacks, loads
  and updates share its lock.
- REG-EVT-019 LIVENESS_MODEL_UPDATE: outcome, version, reason code,
  durationMs, trigger. Codes and numbers only, no URL.
- Debug page: an index URL field, "Check for model update now" (the
  URL and enabled become config overrides) and "Stop model updates".
  Results show in the card and in a snack bar.
- Debug and profile builds only: plain HTTP to 127.0.0.1 and localhost.
  The updater's flag follows LIVENESS_DIAGNOSTICS, and their network
  security config replaces clientmanager's there, keeping its rules.
  Release builds are unchanged: HTTPS only.

Tests: the audit record (1), the holder's refusals and audit (1), and
ModelUpdatesTest (4: settings, scheduling without WorkManager, the kept
outcomes audited once). Module tests 89 -> 95.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
